# SRG-APP-000125-AU-000310  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server system backups must be retained for a minimum of 5
# years for SAMI (Sources and Methods Information) and a minimum of 7 days
# for non-SAMI on media capable of guaranteeing file integrity for the
# minimum applicable information retention period.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000125-AU-000310
group:           V-206459
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           D
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000167 CCI-001348
control_rev5:    AU-11 AU-9

contribution:    The application expresses how long indexed records are held before they
                 roll to frozen, which is the only part of this requirement a Splunk
                 setting reaches, and it can be held to the seven-day floor the check text
                 states.

governs:         indexes.conf - The indexes data is stored in, how large they may grow and how long data
                 is kept.

check:           indexes.conf [<index name>] frozenTimePeriodInSecs min 604800

external:        Selection of backup media capable of guaranteeing file integrity for a
                 minimum of five years, which no Splunk setting expresses
external:        Retention of the backups themselves and the five-year SAMI period,
                 documented in the SSP and carried by the backup tool SPLK-CL-000250 names

citation:        frozenTimePeriodInSecs present cannot fail: indexes.conf.spec:691 gives a
                 default of 188697600, so btool reports the key on every index and the
                 criterion returned a green status that was not evidence. The requirement
                 does state one number the product can be held to - the seven-day non-SAMI
                 floor - and that is not an organization-defined value being invented here
                 but the check text's own words, so a lower bound is both derivable and
                 falsifiable. The five-year figure applies to the backup medium rather than
                 to the index and stays an external dependency.
finding:         An index is configured to roll data to frozen in less than seven days, so
                 the application does not hold the records for the minimum period the
                 requirement states for non-SAMI.
